Location: Pucón, Chile (GMT-3). I'm able to work in different timezones remotely from GMT -8 to GMT +2. Open to relocation and working hybrid or on-site.

Summary
 🎮 I build gameplay features that sound great!

I’m a Technical Sound Designer & Gameplay Engineer with 10+ years and 25+ shipped titles across mobile, PC, and VR. I design, prototype, and ship audio-driven mechanics: systems where audio is not just feedback but game logic (adaptive music/state machines, audio-triggered gameplay events, and spatial/immersive audio that changes gameplay behavior).

Technical highlights:
* Middleware & engines: Wwise, FMOD, Unity (C#), Unreal (Metasounds/BluePrints), and experience integrating audio into large production pipelines.
* Tooling & automation: Wwise File Packager + Addressables/AssetBundles for CI pipelines, editor tools for designers, and automated soundbank workflows.
* Audio craft: field recording/foley, SFX, adaptive music, Dolby Atmos/spatial audio, DAWs (Reaper / Pro Tools / Nuendo).
* Systems & code: C#, C++, Python, build audio managers, low-latency streaming, and gameplay hooks that let audio control or augment mechanics.

🚀 What I bring: I prototype features end-to-end (gameplay + audio), ship performant interactive audio systems, and speak both languages, audio and gameplay engineering, so teams iterate faster and deliver higher fidelity interactions. Open to senior Technical Sound Designer / Audio Programmer / Gameplay Engineer roles focusing on AA/AAA titles where audio and mechanics are tightly coupled.

